    "doc": "config/balance/character.json (version 2); design/narrative/F10-story.md sections 6, 7; config/content/character-names.th.json; studio/decisions/decision-log.md D-146; board detail blocks P2-F10-T04 and P2-F10-T12",
    "_note": "Golden vectors for validateCharacterName(name, params, lexicon) and randomCharacterName(rng, lexicon, params). params = the whole of config/balance/character.json version 2; a vector may carry paramsOverride (dotted path -> value) applied on top. lexicon for vectors = the fixture below, NOT the real content file: it has the same shape as config/content/character-names.th.json (randomName.heads/tails/fallback.names/pattern, blockedTerms.substring.<category>, substringHeavy.terms, token.terms, normalization.allow.light/heavy) so every key path in character.json resolves in both, but the words are neutral placeholders so these vectors do not change when narrative-designer edits the real lists. The fixture exercises every mode: substring (catA, catB, and a _note key that collect must skip), substringHeavy, token, allow.light and allow.heavy. validate expected: ok true -> normalized (the stored string) and graphemes (count after normalize); ok false -> reason, the first failing entry of name.checkOrder (which mode matched is not part of the contract). random: rngDraws are the uniform draws in [0, 1) in the order the rng is called; expected.draws is how many were used, expected.attempts counts template attempts, expected.fallback tells whether the fallback list was used. contentVectors run against the real content file (integration checks, see its _note). Invisible and non-Thai code points are written as \\u escapes. Computed by a scratch reference implementation of character.json (not committed: tools/sim is outside the writes of P2-F10-T04 and P2-H64); version 2 re-checked all 75 version 1 vectors with 0 mismatch before adding the new ones"
  },
